WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:07.340
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Rebels paired up Ezra and Zeb for a very special

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.330
Tie Fighter Field Trip.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.889
Normally I just point out my favorite references
and do a review but I spotted some funny subliminal

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:15.929
messages that I’ll explain too.

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:19.570
If you’re just finding me I’m doing weekly
Rebels videos.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.940
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:26.269
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode but here are my TOP 5 moments.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:29.970
Number 5 - Chopper Robo Trolls Everyone

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.030
The R5 Droid being an asshole provides the
call to action that sets the big Ezra Zeb

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.030
field trip in motion.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.260
But it didn’t stop there.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.160
Later in the episode when Kanan and Hera were
chilling out playing Dejarik, Chopper really

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.070
let them have it.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.330
The scene was a nice reference to the R2 versus
Chewbacca match in Episode 4 with the twist

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.570
that Chopper didn’t have to let Kanan win
for fear of getting his arms ripped out of

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:53.570
their sockets.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.309
When Ezra and Zeb came back he doubled down
on harassing them.

00:00:57.309 --> 00:01:01.230
I’m surprised Zeb didn’t prank him with
a restraining bolt or something.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.030
Troll me once, shame on you, troll me twice,
shame on me.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.640
Number 4 - The Wookiee Life Debt

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.940
They don’t specify how much time has passed
since the last episode, but Ezra is still

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.690
having fun with Zeb for saving his life.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.800
The Wookiee life debt isn’t explained in
the original trilogy really well but the expanded

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.570
universe and the comics picked up the slack.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:24.550
Chewbacca was rescued from an Imperial Prison
Ship by a young Han Solo.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.720
He had been ordered to kill him by his Imperial
supervisor but instead freed Chewie and the

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:34.570
other Wookiees, al lot like the crew of the
Ghost did in the first episode.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.280
When a Wookiee owes their life to someone,
the debt lasts until they are dead.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.850
But I think their children can also choose
to honor it under special circumstances.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:48.430
It’s nice to see them coming together as
a group but Zeb seemed a little too easy to

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:49.430
bait.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.860
He’s not a version of Chewbacca or anything,
but he does fill that role in the crew.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.600
The big scary alien covered in fur.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.950
Yes this is a kid’s show, but I feel like
he would be more fun if they just let him

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.820
be scary and over the course of the series
Ezra won him over.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:10.369
It seems like he wears his emotions on his
sleeves, or wrist bands or whatever he’s

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:11.470
wearing there.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.870
Under normal circumstances, after Ezra and
Chopper busted in on him sleeping, I would

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.720
expect someone with his personality to just
shoot a warning shot at them with a small

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.720
blaster.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.720
Just to scare them off.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.720
We learned last week his entire race was slaughtered
with a few exceptions, so I’m not sensing

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.580
the typical Post Traumatic Stress Behavior
you’d expect.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.349
Number 3 - All For Love of Fruit

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:33.520
They were there for regular supplies, which
they lost.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.870
But Hera trolls them a little with a mission
to nowhere, so she thinks.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:41.099
She wasn’t trying to be mean, but it is
funny to think that everything in the episode

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:45.090
that happened was a result of them being kind
of rotten to each other.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.130
Even Sabine made fun of them with the graffiti
in their room.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.130
It wasn’t her trying to be awful to them.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.880
But in a really subtle way I felt like the
show was telling us all these characters have

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.320
good hearts, but they’re still really selfish.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.000
And if you didn’t catch it in the Dejarik
scene.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.490
Hera and Kanan are totally doing it on the
down low.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.120
They haven’t had a lot of scenes together
in the last 3 episodes.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.710
But there are some trailer clips with them
‘almost kissing’ so you can tell they

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.430
have a relationship that the show will explore
at some point.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:12.280
Hera is one of the few characters we haven’t
spent a lot of time with yet but she and Sabine

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.330
will both get their own episodes soon.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.550
Number 2 - Ezra Learns to Use the Force

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.530
It takes him most of the episode to land the
trick but he’s able to use some limited

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.430
force telekinesis.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:27.340
As of now he’s exhibited near future premonitions,
a force push and now telekenisis.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.659
I guess you could say he’s made some small
force jumps.

00:03:30.659 --> 00:03:36.610
Some of his rooftop acrobatics are a little
superhuman.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.540
We still haven’t seen him train with Kanan’s
lightsaber, I think that will be next.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.560
That and just getting better at the lesser
Jedi powers.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.430
They gave Zeb the Obi-Wan Kenobi line, “This
is not the tie fighter you’re looking for”.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.290
But after some lightsaber training I think
we’ll see Ezra start to learn how to influence

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.350
weaker minds.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:56.470
The stormtroopers on the show are pretty dumb,
so they’ll be easy targets.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:00.739
Of all the Jedi Powers, the ones that allow
you to control others are harder to master.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:04.271
So I’m interested to see if they just let
him do it right away or if he has to work

00:04:04.271 --> 00:04:05.271
up to it.

00:04:05.271 --> 00:04:10.260
If they’re planning on doing a big Ezra
force weilding moment in the finale this year

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.700
it would probably be a lightsaber battle with
the inquisitor.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:19.329
Like the first time luke fought Vader and
got his ass “handed” to him.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:22.740
Ezra is learning to use the force, but he
is light years away from being able to take

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.150
on someone as skilled as the Inquisitor.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.650
I would be pissed if they let him win a lightsaber
battle with him.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.270
Even Anakin Skywalker wasn’t that great
with a lightsaber when he first started.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:33.570
In order for villains to be a threat, they
have to seem unbeatable.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.689
And my Number 1 moment - Tie Fighter Joyrides

00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:41.270
Totally loved them stealing a Tie Fighter,
did not love all the flying through the city.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:45.050
I get that Zeb hadn’t flown one before but
I feel like they let the moment drag on too

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.050
long.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.139
Him talking to Ezra, flying it along side
him while Ezra ran on the roof tops.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:54.569
It felt a little more like a Family Guy gag,
like Peter is flying a Tie Fighter up and

00:04:54.569 --> 00:04:56.800
down the aisles of a grocery store.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.689
Casual Use of Tie Fighters is a funny concept
but I feel like the joke peaked when he was

00:05:00.689 --> 00:05:02.899
spinning it in circles blasting everyone.

00:05:02.899 --> 00:05:06.570
I think they could have cut away sooner and
used the extra time for a scene where the

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.839
imperials punish the farmers for everything.

00:05:08.839 --> 00:05:12.119
They didn’t really follow the rescue idea
through to the logical conclusion.

00:05:12.119 --> 00:05:16.550
Ezra and Zeb crash the tie fighter so the
imperials don’t find them, but then after

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.050
they leave the planet, the imperials just
go back and kill the farmer and his wife.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.139
They were very clearly trying to do the Uncle
Owen Aunt Beru episode 4 scene with the smoldering

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:24.139
ruins.

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:27.710
It’s a kid’s show like I said, so they’re
not going to murder a bunch of people.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:32.830
But don’t you feel like the imperials would
go right back after Ezra and Zeb flew off.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.349
He didn’t destroy their transports.

00:05:34.349 --> 00:05:36.350
Just one of the gun turrets.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.699
They had more weapons.

00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:42.289
And they’re not the only imperials on the
planet.

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:46.229
Part of the theme this week was taking the
quick and easy way will leave you worse off

00:05:46.229 --> 00:05:49.659
than when you started.

00:05:49.659 --> 00:05:54.199
They had the supplies but because Ezra wanted
to steal the fruit they lost everything.

00:05:54.199 --> 00:05:55.620
And even though they saved his farmer friend.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.219
The Empire is still going to take their farm.

00:05:57.219 --> 00:06:01.110
So they didn’t change anything.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.729
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and let me know if you spotted these subliminal

00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:07.289
messages:

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:11.779
I feel like this is a little Disney Propaganda
here but first and most obvious was that you

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:13.050
should eat more fruit.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:16.770
Ezra almost got them killed because he loves
fruit so much.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:20.139
The storm trooper even asked him, “you did
this all for fruit?”

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:22.710
The other big one was when Zeb gave him the
Tie Fighter Helmet.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:27.330
I feel like that’s Disney telling you to
buy more Star Wars toys.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.430
Ezra collects toys, toys cost money, a lot
of money.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.330
Money equals profit.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.749
Anytime I see characters lusting after objects
like they’re toys I feel like it’s merchandising

00:06:37.749 --> 00:06:40.770
for Star Wars toys in real life.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.059
George Lucas made millions of dollars on the
movies, but he made Billions of Dollars on

00:06:45.059 --> 00:06:46.059
the toys.

00:06:46.059 --> 00:06:47.619
The toys are where all the money is.

00:06:47.619 --> 00:06:50.759
Overall I gave the episode a B minus, I feel
like there was a good moral throughline about

00:06:50.759 --> 00:06:54.259
not straying from the path too far and working
together as a team.

00:06:54.259 --> 00:06:57.959
I feel like they’re doing Zeb’s character
a disservice in making him so quick to open

00:06:57.959 --> 00:06:58.959
up to a kid.

00:06:58.959 --> 00:06:59.959
Ezra that is.

00:06:59.959 --> 00:07:04.229
He’s younger than Luke was when he boarded
the Millenium Falcon.

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:09.279
Young children who mostly hang around adults
in cartoons tend to fall into a couple categories.

00:07:09.279 --> 00:07:13.220
They’re either a Bart Simpson character
who gets into mischief all the time, like

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.220
Aladdin.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.679
I know everyone is calling Ezra Space Aladdin.

00:07:16.679 --> 00:07:20.629
Or they’re Meg Griffin and they become the
but of all the jokes.

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:24.209
I don’t think that Ezra is Meg, I do like
the direction they’re taking his character.

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:29.069
But I don’t like it as much when they really
lean hard on the Bart Simpson stuff.

00:07:29.069 --> 00:07:31.580
Stealing the heads off of Stormtroopers and
pranking Zeb.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:35.419
Who I guess in this analogy would be Moe the
Bartender.

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:41.030
I’m really excited to see more of the inquisitor,
who I think is coming back in episode 4 next

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.030
week.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:46.539
Since Monday nights I’m usually working
on Gotham, I’ll just be posting Rebels videos

00:07:46.539 --> 00:07:51.319
on Tuesdays, so be sure to subscribe to get
everything.

00:07:51.319 --> 00:07:57.060
There’s a lot going on this week with the
new Legend of Korra game, I’ll be streaming

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.060
that.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:02.110
So check the description for those links.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:08.770
Right now click here for Rebels Episode 2
and click here to catch up on Legend of Korra.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:12.409
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and stream some Korra.

